<h4><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Multi-Genre_combinations">Multi-Genre=
 combinations</span></h4>
<p>The only way to get a "Great Combo" for multi-genre games is to use two =
genres that when used on their own with the chosen topic result in a "Great=
 Combo". This means that topics like Surgery can not get "Great Combo" on m=
ulti-genre games. <a class=3D"mw-redirect" href=3D"https://gamedevtycoon.fa=
ndom.com/wiki/Review_Algorithm#Combination_study" title=3D"Review Algorithm=
">-source</a>
</p>
<h4><span id=3D"Topic.2FAudience_combinations"></span><span class=3D"mw-hea=
dline" id=3D"Topic/Audience_combinations">Topic/Audience combinations</span=
></h4>
<p>You will occasionally get messages about matches or mismatches of target=
 audience and platform you have chosen. Your choice of audience <b>primaril=
y affects the number of sales</b> your game will generate. The higher the s=
ales modifier of the selected Topic is, the more sales you will get with th=
at target audience. <a class=3D"mw-redirect" href=3D"https://gamedevtycoon.=
fandom.com/wiki/Review_Algorithm#Final_Score_calculation_and_post-treatment=
" title=3D"Review Algorithm">-source</a>
</p><p>These combinations are covered in the table above.
</p>
<h3><span id=3D"Platform.2FGenre_combinations"></span><span class=3D"mw-hea=
dline" id=3D"Platform/Genre_combinations">Platform/Genre combinations</span=
></h3>
<p>Each genre has its own popularity on each platform. Your choice of genre=
, relative to platform, slightly affects the review scores. The higher the =
sales modifier of the selected platform, the more sales you will get with t=
hat genre.
</p><p>When you develop a <a href=3D"https://gamedevtycoon.fandom.com/wiki/=
Custom_Console" title=3D"Custom Console">Custom Console</a>, the genre and =
audience combinations are generated based on your list of previously releas=
ed games; they aren't predetermined like the standard consoles. They are th=
erefore different between one playthrough and another, and even potentially=
 different between one custom console and another within the same playthrou=
gh.<br>
For genres, your two most frequently used genres will be <span style=3D"bac=
kground-color:rgb(50,150,50); padding: 0 5px;">+++</span> (Great), your thi=
rd most frequently used genre will be <span style=3D"background-color:rgb(6=
0,120,60); padding: 0 5px;">++</span> (Good), fourth and fifth will be <spa=
n style=3D"background-color:rgb(70,90,70); padding: 0 5px;">+</span> (Okay)=
, and sixth/least frequently used <span style=3D"background-color:rgb(120,6=
0,60); padding: 0 5px;">=E2=88=92=E2=88=92</span> (Bad).<br>
For audiences, your most frequently used audience will be <span style=3D"ba=
ckground-color:rgb(50,150,50); padding: 0 5px;">+++</span> (Great), second =
most frequently used <span style=3D"background-color:rgb(60,120,60); paddin=
g: 0 5px;">++</span> (Good), and least frequently used <span style=3D"backg=
round-color:rgb(70,90,70); padding: 0 5px;">+</span> (Okay).
</p>
