v class=3D"comment__body"><p>... And this is why people get better on "gut"=
 feeling sometimes.
</p><p>Statistically, you are more likely to land somewhere in the middle i=
f you act randomly, but without much deviation (and if you have no knowledg=
e of game workings you are pretty much acting randomly, but since you use c=
ommon sense you aren't doing totall bullshit like releasing a hospital rpg =
mature on gameling). Therefore, you are consistent, and that is what matter=
s!
</p><p>However, once you try to use this information, if you misunderstand =
some of it, you will start getting good sometimes and bad sometimes, thus y=
ou will start seeing more bad scores (because your failures would be compar=
ed to your perfect wins, not your medicore results to your medicore results=
)
</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
