09:56 UTC</span> <span class=3D"comment__edited">(edited)</span></div><div =
class=3D"comment__body"><p>Development Focus is not directly for sliders. W=
hen in that raw data table is higher value it simply means that your slloca=
ted time - horizontal bar (not slider) have to be: 0.9+ =3D 40%+, 0.61-0.89=
 =3D 21-39% and 0.6 is 20% and lower.
</p><p>When multi-genre You take 2x value for the first genre + second genr=
e value then devide by 2 and multiply by 0.6666, value you get then is unde=
r criteria I wrote above.
</p><p>With this procedure you can easily get 7+ rating, of course your pla=
tform/genre combination have to be good. Getting really top ratings is much=
 harder because one of the things that matter the most are tech/design rati=
os and those are hard to achieve because your staff stats are influencing i=
t very much also as speed boosts and how you allocate your staff to tasks.
</p></div></div>
<div class=3D"comment reply"><div class=3D"comment__meta"><span class=3D"co=
mment__author">A Fandom user</span> <span class=3D"comment__date">2013-05-0=
2 10:54 UTC</span> <span class=3D"comment__edited">(edited)</span></div><di=
v class=3D"comment__body"><p>Actually, the decisions are a bit different:
</p><p>0.9 or more &gt; over 20% to avoid penalty, over 40% to get bonus
</p><p>under 0.8- &gt; <b>under</b> 40% to avoid penalty
</p><p>0.8 itself is like a joker - you can assign as much (or as little) a=
s you want.
</p></div></div>
